// Between Frontiers: rules of influence (phase 4). Contract: crates/bf-sim/src/influence.rs
// (InfluenceRules); design: docs/influence.pt-BR.md (sections 3, 4, 11 and 13). Licence:
// CC BY-SA 4.0.
//
// DESIGN CHOICES, to balance after phase 6 (the owner's rule: features before balance). Per
// mille throughout.
//
// - Dependence of B on A, channel by channel: the flow over B's GDP times A's share of that
//   channel in B (vulnerability, Keohane and Nye 1977). Only credit is live; investment, trade and
//   protection are dormant until their fronts exist.
// - Influence counts by issue (Baldwin 1979): each issue weighs the channels its own way. The
//   issue of a proposal is its dominant term in the treaties' valuation. Goodwill counts the same
//   in every issue.
// - Goodwill keeps 917 per mille a year: half in 8 years (0.917^8 = 0.50). Aid buys a vote only
//   while it lasts and a little after (Kuziemko and Werker 2006).
// - Affinity multiplies, weakly (Walt 1987: alignment follows threat more than ideology): from 800
//   (opposite regimes, no people in common) to 1200 (same laws, a large community of A's main
//   culture in B); the people term is full at 20 % of B's people.
(
    issues: [
        // A creditor weighs in money; an investor in money and trade; a protector in security.
        (issue: Money, credit: 1000, investment: 600, trade: 300, protection: 0),
        (issue: Trade, credit: 200, investment: 600, trade: 1000, protection: 0),
        (issue: Territory, credit: 200, investment: 300, trade: 200, protection: 600),
        (issue: Security, credit: 100, investment: 100, trade: 100, protection: 1000),
        (issue: Sovereignty, credit: 400, investment: 400, trade: 400, protection: 800),
    ],
    goodwill_yearly_retention: 917,
    affinity_floor: 800,
    affinity_ceiling: 1200,
    regime_weight: 500,
    people_weight: 500,
    people_full: 200,
    // In a proposal of A that B weighs, A's influence over B adds influence × B's GDP × this.
    proposal_weight: 1000,
    // The term never adds more than this share of the proposal's size: a patron's influence makes
    // a country accept a small loss, never any loss.
    proposal_cap: 250,
    // Trade and investment channels (docs/influence.pt-BR.md, 13c): off until the PR that turns
    // them on, judged by itself on the aggregates.
    live_ties: false,
    // The foreign service (section 12): missions of 1925 by rule (the Correlates of War data may
    // not be redistributed), teams for simultaneous negotiations, an act without a mission yields
    // half, and administrative efficiency (computers) adds up to as many teams again.
    // Rapprochement with a regime the groups that count reject costs up to 200 per mille of
    // legitimacy (the politics' stance unit is 500).
    service: (
        great_powers: 7,
        missions_per_team: 10,
        without_mission: 500,
        efficiency_gain: 1000,
        domestic_weight: 200,
        stance_unit: 500,
    ),
    source: "docs/influence.pt-BR.md, sections 3, 4 and 11; Hirschman 1945; Keohane and Nye 1977; Baldwin 1979; Walt 1987; Kuziemko and Werker 2006",
)
